content.text:
The FAQ at 767px (max-width: 767px) should have `padding-top: 52px; padding-bottom: 72px`. Current CSS has `padding-top: 52px; padding-bottom: 72px` — that matches. But wait, the drift is -59px (local is 59px shorter), meaning we need more height. The padding-bottom 72px should be there. Let me re-read current faq CSS at 767px:

Looking at our current faq-section.module.css:
```
@media screen and (max-width: 767px) {
  .faqSection {
    padding-top: 52px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }
```

That matches Webflow exactly. The -59px at 768 must come from something else. At 768, it might be due to the grid stacking differently. Let me look at the faq outer grid at 991px — the Webflow has a 2-col grid at 991px. Our current CSS at 991px:

```css
@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {
  .faqSection {
    padding-top: 60px;
  }

  .fqOuterGrid {
    grid-column-gap: 50px;
    grid-row-gap: 50px;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    align-items: center;
  }
```

At 768px the grid becomes flex-column. The -59px at 768 might be a `faqWrapperLarge` padding issue. Let me check Webflow at 991px for faq-wrapper-large:

