content.text:
The FAQ CSS at 767px has `padding-top: 52px; padding-bottom: 72px` which matches Webflow. The -59px at 768 is likely from the **outer grid** collapsing to single column from the 2-col layout, which adds a 50px row gap becoming vertical stacking. But the measurements show local is SHORTER at 768 — meaning we're missing content height.

Let me check what happens at 768px: The grid at `max-width: 767px` collapses to `flex-flow: column` (single column). The 2 columns stack vertically. In Webflow the `grid-row-gap: 50px` adds 50px when stacked. Currently our CSS at 767px removes the grid gap (it becomes `flex-flow: column` with no explicit gap). Let me check our current CSS:

Looking at current faq-section.module.css at 767px:
```css
@media screen and (max-width: 767px) {
  .faqSection {
    padding-top: 52px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }
  .fqOuterGrid {
    display: flex;
    flex-flow: column;
    grid-column-gap: unset;
    grid-row-gap: unset;
  }
```

We unset the row-gap. In Webflow at 767px:

